    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule on the owner create endpoint. When a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a **different** telephone, it is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the Owner schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). The `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this at build time.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `possibleDuplicateOf` column (Integer) with getter/setter, alongside the existing derived-on-create fields (`customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`).\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the nullable `possible_duplicate_of` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignored the two new targets so they're populated in the controller (matching the existing `bulkSignupWarning`/`identityKey` pattern).\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicateOf(Owner)`, which runs *after* the hard-duplicate check has passed and returns the id of the first existing owner sharing last name (case-insensitive) and postcode with a different canonical telephone, or `null`. The value is stored on the owner at create time, and `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields` sets `possibleDuplicate = (id != null)` and `possibleDuplicateOf = id` on both the create and read responses.\n\nBecause the match is captured at creation and persisted, `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the stable `possibleDuplicateOf` pointing to the pre-existing owner (not a symmetric read-time recomputation) \u2014 matching the spec's \"shares an existing owner's\" semantics.",
